 REFERENCES OF TENSOR DETERMINATION METHODS :
 INVDIR : DIRECT INVERSION. - modified from a first
  method, now abandoned, by J. Angelier and J. Goguel
  (1979) [C.R.Acad.Sci.Paris,288,(D),307-310], based on
  analytic inversion ; the present method INVDIR
  minimizes a function thay depends on both the slip-
  shear angle and the shear. This function resembles the
  function described as S4 by J. Angelier (1984) [Journal of
  Geophys.Res.,89,B7,5835-5848]. The new method INVDIR is
  described in detail in J.Angelier (1988),
  Geophysical J. International, 103, 363-376.
 R4DT, R4DS, R2DT, R2DS : ITERATIVE SEARCH. -
  These methods imply search of stress axes
  in 2 (R2DT,R2DS) or 4 dimensions (R4DT,R4DS),
  as well as of ratio PHI. First presentation in :
  J.Angelier (1975), C.R.Acad.Sci.Paris, 281,(D), 1805-1808
  [erratum, 283,(D),p.466]. More detailed descriptions in :
  J.Angelier (1979a) [Tectonophysics,56,T17-T26];
  J.Angelier (1979b) [Soc.Geol.Nord,Publ.3,418p.,29pl];
  J.Angelier (1983) [Soc.Geol.France,7,XXV,5,661-672];
  J.Angelier (1984) [J. of Geophys.Res.,89,B7,5835-5848].
  In the iterative search, the functions adopted are
  S2 (R4DTAN) or S3 (R4DSIN) : J.Angelier (1984,p.5841)
  These functions minimize the stria-shear angle solely, so
  that permutations of axes may occur for special data sets.
  For R2DS/R2DT, one axis is constrained to vertical.

 APPLICATIONS ET AUTRES METHODES. -
  Detailed practical examples of tensor determinations,
  in addition to papers mentioned above, are given in :
  J.Angelier, B.Colletta and R.E.Anderson (1985) [Geol. Soc.
    Amer. Bull. 96, 347-361 and Suppl. Data 85-09];
  J.Angelier (1989) [J. Struct. Geol.,11,1/2,37-50];
  Other methods are used in different programs,
  such as :  DIEDRE (method of P- and T- dihedra),
             CONJUG (analysis of conjugate systems).
  Furthermore, special programs allow additional analyses
  following this program : ANATEN, TRIAGE, DIMOHR.

